      "artist": "Alan Wilson from Peterborough, Cambs, UK",
      "description": "BAC Jet Provost, c/n PAC/W/6307.  Built in 1958 and served with the RAF College Cranwell, then No.1 and No.7 Flying Training Schools (1FTS &amp; 7FTS).  Retired in 1989 and with the fire section at RAF Church Fenton by May 1990 with the maintenance serial 9036M.  Joined the museum in 1995.  South Yorkshire Air Museum, Doncaster, South Yorkshire, UK, 7th August 2020.",
